    {
      "v": 1,
      "zh": "约旦河西亚摩利人的诸王和靠海迦南人的诸王，听见耶和华在以色列人前面使约旦河的水干了，等到我们过去，他们的心因以色列人的缘故就消化了，不再有胆气。",
      "en": "When all the Amorite kings on the west side of the Jordan and all the Canaanite kings along the seacoast heard how the Lord had dried up the water of the Jordan before the Israelites while they[NOTE:1] crossed, they lost their courage and could not even breathe for fear of the Israelites.[NOTE:2]",
      "notes": [
        "Another textual tradition has, “while we crossed.”",
        "Heb “their heart[s] melted and there was no longer in them breath (or perhaps “spirit”) because of the sons of Israel.”"
